# Android 17 Razr sun engineering DSU: restore two OEM Bluetooth/FM DAI
# backend modules missing in r44/r45, but present on the same stock OEM kernel.
# The upstream Motorola modules and ABI are unchanged. Kernel module insertion
# uses the OEM modprobe SELinux domain. It resolves dependencies and executes
# sequentially; failures remain visible in init logs and never claim readiness.
# Trigger only for exactly the tested sun / SDK37 combination.
on property:ro.boot.product.vendor.sku=sun && property:ro.build.version.sdk=37
    exec u:r:vendor_modprobe:s0 -- /vendor/bin/modprobe -b -s -d /vendor_dlkm/lib/modules -a btfmcodec btfm_slim_codec bt_fm_swr
